1
00:01:36,150 --> 00:01:40,080
[River of No Return]

2
00:01:40,150 --> 00:01:43,020
[Episode 16: Escape From Prison]

3
00:01:46,150 --> 00:01:47,680
Help me with this one first.

4
00:01:49,009 --> 00:01:50,810
We'll talk about the rest later.

5
00:01:52,390 --> 00:01:53,560
You'd better keep your word.

6
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:54,360
I swear I will.

7
00:01:56,570 --> 00:01:59,630
The man you're looking for, Wang Teng,
is already dead.

8
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:01,880
There are constables in the yard.

9
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:20,890
What's this for?

10
00:02:21,270 --> 00:02:22,170
Tingyi,

11
00:02:22,550 --> 00:02:24,450
this riot is a serious matter,

12
00:02:24,470 --> 00:02:25,790
no matter who orchestrated it.

13
00:02:25,790 --> 00:02:27,240
If you hadn't warned us,

14
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:29,730
the Grand Canal might've been
brought to a standstill.

15
00:02:29,730 --> 00:02:30,400
Fang,

16
00:02:31,329 --> 00:02:33,450
no need for formalities between us.

17
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:37,010
I see you've come back

18
00:02:37,010 --> 00:02:38,270
having found nothing.

19
00:02:39,020 --> 00:02:40,210
Now, can you tell me

20
00:02:40,430 --> 00:02:42,560
exactly what you've been looking for?

21
00:02:53,610 --> 00:02:54,810
Everyone, remember.

22
00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:56,730
If the judicial commissioner asks,

23
00:02:56,730 --> 00:02:58,190
push all the blame onto me.

24
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:00,660
No one died, after all.

25
00:03:00,670 --> 00:03:02,330
So it's not a capital offense.

26
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:04,340
At worst, I'll get a beating.

27
00:03:05,270 --> 00:03:06,450
But from now on,

28
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:08,510
we'll finally have enough to eat.

29
00:03:08,510 --> 00:03:09,610
Small price to pay.

30
00:03:10,060 --> 00:03:10,560
Kong,

31
00:03:10,730 --> 00:03:12,270
a man should take responsibility
for his own actions.

32
00:03:12,270 --> 00:03:13,860
How could we push it all onto you?

33
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:14,930
Why not?

34
00:03:15,170 --> 00:03:17,630
We agreed on this
before we acted, didn't we?

35
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:18,890
It's fine.

36
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:21,620
I have no family to worry about.

37
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:23,829
Even if it costs me my life,
it'd still be worth it.

38
00:03:23,829 --> 00:03:24,430
It's fine.

39
00:03:24,610 --> 00:03:25,810
If I were the Emperor,

40
00:03:26,110 --> 00:03:28,340
I'd abolish this wretched
canal transport system altogether.

41
00:03:28,340 --> 00:03:29,400
Then we wouldn't have to

42
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:30,800
suffer exploitation anymore.

43
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:31,600
That's right.

44
00:03:31,930 --> 00:03:32,790
Without the canal transport system,

45
00:03:32,790 --> 00:03:33,540
the local offices along the route

46
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:34,890
wouldn't need to conscript labor anymore.

47
00:03:34,890 --> 00:03:35,620
Then we could

48
00:03:35,630 --> 00:03:37,170
all go home and farm in peace.

49
00:03:37,170 --> 00:03:37,730
Yeah,

50
00:03:37,750 --> 00:03:39,790
and we wouldn't have to
put up with Xue Baguan anymore.

51
00:03:39,790 --> 00:03:40,840
I heard Xue Baguan

52
00:03:40,990 --> 00:03:42,510
has been lining his pockets
by skimming our rations

53
00:03:42,510 --> 00:03:43,470
to pay for a long-term stay

54
00:03:43,470 --> 00:03:45,470
in the best room at Zuihong Brothel.

55
00:03:47,180 --> 00:03:47,990
Where's Hong?

56
00:03:55,260 --> 00:03:56,050
Hong.

57
00:03:57,960 --> 00:04:00,690
What are you thinking about
all alone here again?

58
00:04:00,710 --> 00:04:01,570
Come on, get up.

59
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:03,580
Wipe yourself off. Hurry.

60
00:04:05,230 --> 00:04:05,800
Here.

61
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:11,000
Thank you.

62
00:04:12,070 --> 00:04:14,930
You don't seem like
a child from an ordinary family.

63
00:04:16,410 --> 00:04:17,490
Don't be nervous.

64
00:04:18,589 --> 00:04:19,910
Behind closed doors,

65
00:04:20,529 --> 00:04:21,490
every family has a little something

66
00:04:21,490 --> 00:04:23,020
they'd rather keep hidden,

67
00:04:23,170 --> 00:04:23,800
right?

68
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:32,610
You asked me earlier
whether I'd served in the army.

69
00:04:32,610 --> 00:04:34,740
Your eyes are sharper than a falcon's.

70
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:39,120
I guessed right, then.

71
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:42,860
That's right.

72
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:45,820
My hometown is in Huai'an.

73
00:04:46,909 --> 00:04:50,640
When I was young, I was conscripted into
the Prince of Yan's forces.

74
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:54,180
Later, I served as a scout
in the Xinghe Battalion.

75
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:14,670
Those men over there were like me.

76
00:05:19,260 --> 00:05:21,790
We were injured
during the campaign that year

77
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:24,820
and could never return to the battlefield.

78
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:27,420
As a scout,
you can't afford to be slow to react.

79
00:05:28,530 --> 00:05:30,930
The army wanted to
keep me as an instructor.

80
00:05:31,670 --> 00:05:33,270
But I was getting on in years.

81
00:05:34,370 --> 00:05:35,640
So I left the military

82
00:05:35,670 --> 00:05:37,070
and came back to Huai'an.

83
00:05:37,550 --> 00:05:38,810
There are many of my old comrades here,

84
00:05:38,810 --> 00:05:40,610
so we can look out for each other.

85
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:42,590
After years on the frontier,

86
00:05:42,590 --> 00:05:43,930
I've seen too much.

87
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:45,530
I can't

88
00:05:47,050 --> 00:05:48,530
tell them these things.

89
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:52,580
Even if I did, they wouldn't understand.

90
00:05:56,650 --> 00:05:57,610
But I believe

91
00:05:59,340 --> 00:06:00,340
you will.

92
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:03,160
What they said just now was wrong.

93
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,940
There's no counting the abuses

94
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:09,290
along this canal.

95
00:06:10,470 --> 00:06:14,330
But if we abolish the north-south canal transport
because of this...

96
00:06:14,550 --> 00:06:16,010
What's that saying again?

97
00:06:17,730 --> 00:06:20,330
"Don't throw the baby out
with the bathwater."

98
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:28,530
Those wealthy merchants

99
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:31,120
oppose moving the capital

100
00:06:33,070 --> 00:06:34,870
because they profit enormously

101
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:36,800
from the canal transport.

102
00:06:39,740 --> 00:06:41,340
But would the common people,

103
00:06:41,550 --> 00:06:43,080
who toil so hard at the dams,

104
00:06:43,760 --> 00:06:45,240
really think the same way?

105
00:06:50,909 --> 00:06:53,240
When you've spent enough time in the army,

106
00:06:53,850 --> 00:06:57,300
you start thinking about
more than just filling your stomach.

107
00:06:57,300 --> 00:06:59,290
I spent many years on the frontier.

108
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:03,320
The border troubles have never ceased.

109
00:07:05,680 --> 00:07:08,140
The powers on the steppe
are like wild grass:

110
00:07:08,170 --> 00:07:09,700
one rises as another falls.

111
00:07:10,060 --> 00:07:11,920
There are the Tatars, the Oirats,

112
00:07:12,470 --> 00:07:13,610
and the Uriankhai.

113
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:15,410
Just when we'd brought Arughtai to heel,

114
00:07:15,410 --> 00:07:16,800
Mahmud popped up.

115
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:19,830
Just when we'd brought Mahmud to heel,

116
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:22,010
that same Arughtai turned on us again.

117
00:07:25,550 --> 00:07:28,080
The steppe has always
belonged to the strong.

118
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:29,800
When you're strong,

119
00:07:29,910 --> 00:07:31,370
they keep their distance.

120
00:07:32,030 --> 00:07:33,630
But the moment you grow weak,

121
00:07:33,650 --> 00:07:34,850
they pounce.

122
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:37,730
The balance of power
is constantly shifting.

123
00:08:48,910 --> 00:08:51,050
Who exactly did Commander Wang
have a feud with?

124
00:08:51,050 --> 00:08:52,800
Were the household's guests
carefully screened?

125
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:53,930
You're his steward.

126
00:08:54,340 --> 00:08:55,600
How could you not know?

127
00:08:58,530 --> 00:09:00,190
Are you going to tell us or not?

128
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:03,930
Enough.

129
00:09:04,510 --> 00:09:06,710
We won't get anything useful out of him.

130
00:09:08,270 --> 00:09:09,270
Seventh Brother,

131
00:09:09,550 --> 00:09:11,940
Lord Wang died
with blood streaming from all 7 orifices.

132
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:13,540
He was definitely poisoned.

133
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:16,610
You can't just lie through your teeth.

134
00:09:17,130 --> 00:09:17,800
Boss,

135
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:19,510
look at this plaque.

136
00:09:20,120 --> 00:09:22,380
This is an honor bestowed by the Emperor.

137
00:09:22,580 --> 00:09:23,910
What day was yesterday?

138
00:09:24,180 --> 00:09:25,960
It was the late Consort Jing's birthday.

139
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:28,100
This is a genuine imperial case.

140
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:31,200
Is a case this big
something you and I can investigate?

141
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,530
Dozens of guests

142
00:09:32,890 --> 00:09:34,340
were all served the same food.

143
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:37,370
But why was Lord Wang
the only one who died?

144
00:09:37,530 --> 00:09:39,190
The culprit could've poisoned him any day,

145
00:09:39,190 --> 00:09:42,990
yet he chose to do it at his daughter's
posthumous birthday banquet.

146
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:44,930
That plaque is new,

147
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:47,420
and the memorial tablet
for Consort Jing is also new.

148
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:50,080
If you ask me,
we should start with his daughter.

149
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:51,220
Buddy,

150
00:09:52,170 --> 00:09:54,820
Consort Jing
was already buried with the late Emperor.

151
00:09:54,820 --> 00:09:56,820
How could we possibly investigate?

152
00:10:06,910 --> 00:10:07,720
Dr. Su?

153
00:10:08,180 --> 00:10:08,930
You're...

154
00:10:10,130 --> 00:10:11,530
not a constable anymore?

155
00:10:12,970 --> 00:10:14,110
You don't look

156
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:15,900
much like a doctor either.

157
00:10:16,630 --> 00:10:17,890
What are you doing at a dead man's house,

158
00:10:17,890 --> 00:10:19,010
treating the dead?

159
00:10:21,060 --> 00:10:22,410
This is not a place to talk.

160
00:10:22,410 --> 00:10:22,940
Let's go.

161
00:10:55,130 --> 00:10:55,770
Come in.

162
00:11:12,510 --> 00:11:13,570
What is this place?

163
00:11:14,150 --> 00:11:16,280
You haven't answered my question yet.

164
00:11:16,750 --> 00:11:18,220
Why have you come to Huai'an?

165
00:11:18,220 --> 00:11:20,200
Would you believe me
if I said I was just passing through?

166
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:21,600
Do you think I'd buy that?

167
00:11:22,060 --> 00:11:24,260
Then what's your theory, Constable Wu?

168
00:11:26,010 --> 00:11:27,650
I caught a whiff

169
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:29,170
of death on you just now.

170
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:34,730
Nonsense. It's clearly
just the herbal fragrance.

171
00:11:34,730 --> 00:11:35,560
I'm not a coroner.

172
00:11:35,560 --> 00:11:37,090
How come I smell of the dead?

173
00:11:44,410 --> 00:11:45,530
A hint of smoke

174
00:11:45,930 --> 00:11:47,260
and a hint of clear wine.

175
00:11:48,540 --> 00:11:50,540
You went to pay respects to the dead.

176
00:11:50,670 --> 00:11:51,410
Who was it?

177
00:11:52,050 --> 00:11:53,580
What are you, a bloodhound?

178
00:11:55,480 --> 00:12:00,130
Was it Consort Jing—the woman
whose posthumous birthday banquet

179
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:02,930
those people were just talking about?

180
00:12:02,950 --> 00:12:04,340
She had a name of her own.

181
00:12:05,550 --> 00:12:07,010
Her name was Wang Jingshu.

182
00:12:07,930 --> 00:12:09,680
She was only 19 when she died.

183
00:12:11,530 --> 00:12:13,080
So you were the one

184
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:15,650
who poisoned Wang Teng?

185
00:12:16,220 --> 00:12:16,720
Yes.

186
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:18,770
I poisoned him.

187
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:21,300
Are you going to arrest me?

188
00:12:22,410 --> 00:12:24,070
I'm a constable from Jinling.

189
00:12:24,370 --> 00:12:26,570
I have no jurisdiction here in Huai'an.

190
00:12:27,390 --> 00:12:28,480
He sold his own daughter

191
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:29,960
for wealth and glory.

192
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:32,380
He deserved to die.

193
00:12:33,050 --> 00:12:35,250
So is that why you've been so determined

194
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:37,160
to follow Old Mule to Beijing?

195
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:38,770
For revenge?

196
00:12:40,130 --> 00:12:43,660
I want to change this cruel system
that devours people's lives.

197
00:12:45,430 --> 00:12:47,290
You're just a lowly doctor.

198
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:50,160
How are you going to change
the Zhu family's rules?

199
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:51,900
How will I know unless I try?

200
00:12:56,650 --> 00:12:57,220
True.

201
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:00,960
But now Old Mule has been captured.

202
00:13:01,460 --> 00:13:04,120
Have you thought about
how to get to the capital?

203
00:13:09,410 --> 00:13:12,610
Isn't that why you're dressed like this?
To go rescue him?

204
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:20,970
If you hadn't talked me into following

205
00:13:21,370 --> 00:13:22,770
Old Mule back in Jinling,

206
00:13:24,560 --> 00:13:25,800
I don't know

207
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:27,580
where I'd be right now.

208
00:13:28,270 --> 00:13:28,960
Yeah.

209
00:13:31,870 --> 00:13:34,600
Who knows
if we're fated to meet or fated to clash?

210
00:13:36,770 --> 00:13:39,170
After all this time, we meet here again.

211
00:13:44,570 --> 00:13:46,700
Do you still want to go back to Jinling?

212
00:13:53,030 --> 00:13:53,890
I can't go back.

213
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:04,500
Neither of us can go back.

214
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:17,040
Do you have a brush?

215
00:14:38,990 --> 00:14:39,720
You write it.

216
00:14:41,170 --> 00:14:43,890
My handwriting... isn't very good.

217
00:14:45,030 --> 00:14:46,560
I don't know how to write
an official document.

218
00:14:46,560 --> 00:14:47,200
I do.

219
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:49,200
I'll dictate, and you write.

220
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:50,740
♪ Along the Qinhuai River in Nanjing ♪

221
00:14:50,790 --> 00:14:52,290
♪ I patrol the streets,
swaying along day after day ♪

222
00:14:52,520 --> 00:14:54,050
♪ A jug of wine in hand,
a blade of grass between my teeth ♪

223
00:14:54,070 --> 00:14:55,680
♪ Even the rowdiest ghosts run
when they see me ♪

224
00:14:55,880 --> 00:14:57,380
♪ Through storms and flames, I press on ♪

225
00:14:57,480 --> 00:14:59,000
♪ I drag my life along like a rope ♪

226
00:14:59,030 --> 00:15:00,580
♪ They call me a young constable ♪

227
00:15:00,610 --> 00:15:02,210
♪ But this realm isn't mine to rule ♪

228
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:03,770
♪ Isn't mine to rule ♪

229
00:15:16,630 --> 00:15:17,800
All I know is this:

230
00:15:19,060 --> 00:15:20,860
now, the capital and the Emperor

231
00:15:21,530 --> 00:15:22,650
stand behind

232
00:15:22,670 --> 00:15:24,000
the northern frontier.

233
00:15:24,050 --> 00:15:25,580
So the supplies delivered by canal,

234
00:15:25,580 --> 00:15:27,650
such as provisions and weapons,

235
00:15:27,870 --> 00:15:29,170
never run short.

236
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:31,030
The frontier walls are also

237
00:15:31,650 --> 00:15:34,310
built solidly enough
to deter foreign enemies.

238
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:39,300
If the Emperor moves
the capital to Jinling,

239
00:15:40,580 --> 00:15:41,640
what would happen?

240
00:15:43,960 --> 00:15:45,620
Even if the court moves south,

241
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:50,380
a senior general or a vassal king
would remain in the north.

242
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:54,970
Everything could continue
according to the old system.

243
00:15:56,050 --> 00:15:57,180
That wouldn't work.

244
00:15:59,530 --> 00:16:02,840
Even if you brought Xu Da and Chang Yuchun
back from the dead,

245
00:16:02,840 --> 00:16:04,170
it still wouldn't work.

246
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:06,960
Why did Emperor Yongle move the capital

247
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:09,170
to Beiping, so close to the steppe?

248
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:10,640
Because he knew that

249
00:16:11,960 --> 00:16:14,600
only when the emperor personally
guards the gates of the realm

250
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:17,330
can the border soldiers
have a pillar of strength

251
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:18,890
and hold their ground.

252
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:28,090
You really think so?

253
00:16:35,190 --> 00:16:36,450
I never expected that,

254
00:16:37,620 --> 00:16:40,480
while bearing the heavy burden
of canal transport,

255
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:43,480
you'd still care about
keeping the frontier at peace.

256
00:16:44,250 --> 00:16:45,650
I've learned a lot today.

257
00:16:47,410 --> 00:16:49,070
That's just how soldiers are.

258
00:16:56,630 --> 00:16:57,320
Indeed.

259
00:16:58,930 --> 00:17:00,170
Where the emperor is,

260
00:17:00,910 --> 00:17:02,600
there lies the strength of the realm.

261
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:03,320
Well said.

262
00:17:04,869 --> 00:17:06,069
Where the emperor is,

263
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:09,079
there lies the strength of the realm.

264
00:17:11,700 --> 00:17:13,630
Emperor Yongle must've explained

265
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:17,130
the intention
behind his decision to you, right?

266
00:17:18,329 --> 00:17:19,280
Back then,

267
00:17:20,869 --> 00:17:21,760
my grandfather

268
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:24,450
said them...

269
00:17:39,450 --> 00:17:40,510
Too many eyes and ears here,

270
00:17:40,510 --> 00:17:42,440
so I can't pay you proper respects.

271
00:17:43,260 --> 00:17:45,190
Please forgive me, Your Highness.

272
00:17:57,600 --> 00:17:59,000
How did you recognize me?

273
00:18:00,330 --> 00:18:01,090
That year,

274
00:18:01,630 --> 00:18:04,290
when Your Highness
accompanied Emperor Yongle

275
00:18:04,310 --> 00:18:07,500
on the northern campaign, the Xinghe Battalion
specially dispatched a cavalry unit

276
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:09,200
to guard your camp from afar.

277
00:18:10,170 --> 00:18:11,370
I was one of them.

278
00:18:13,610 --> 00:18:15,440
Scouts all have very sharp eyes.

279
00:18:16,570 --> 00:18:18,330
We had to commit

280
00:18:18,350 --> 00:18:20,440
Your Highness's appearance to memory.

281
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:21,280
So,

282
00:18:22,170 --> 00:18:25,100
I took the liberty of
testing my suspicions just now.

283
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:28,870
Please forgive me, Your Highness.

284
00:18:34,070 --> 00:18:34,610
Sit.

285
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:50,000
Your Highness, you must have your reasons

286
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,540
for coming here in disguise.

287
00:18:51,540 --> 00:18:53,270
You need not explain them to me.

288
00:18:53,760 --> 00:18:55,820
But there is one thing I'd like to ask.

289
00:18:57,780 --> 00:18:59,980
I hope Your Highness will enlighten me.

290
00:19:05,760 --> 00:19:06,480
Go ahead.

291
00:19:07,540 --> 00:19:09,940
It was truly an accident
that Your Highness

292
00:19:10,630 --> 00:19:12,200
fell in with us

293
00:19:12,780 --> 00:19:14,440
and wound up in prison, right?

294
00:19:23,310 --> 00:19:23,940
Yes.

295
00:19:35,810 --> 00:19:37,520
This old soldier, Kong Shiba,

296
00:19:38,070 --> 00:19:39,800
is at Your Highness's command.

297
00:19:43,650 --> 00:19:44,440
Kong.

298
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:48,960
Please rise.

299
00:19:56,660 --> 00:19:57,270
Come on.

300
00:20:13,260 --> 00:20:15,380
[Huai'an Branch of
the Ministry of Justice]

301
00:20:20,260 --> 00:20:21,610
We're from the Huai'an Guard.

302
00:20:21,610 --> 00:20:22,410
Open the gate.

303
00:20:28,280 --> 00:20:30,340
Under orders from the Huai'an Guard,

304
00:20:30,410 --> 00:20:33,070
I'm here to take custody of
the ringleaders of the riot at the dam.

305
00:20:33,070 --> 00:20:35,730
This is Dr. Su,
the medical officer of the guard.

306
00:20:35,930 --> 00:20:38,570
If the prisoners
have any injuries or illnesses,

307
00:20:38,570 --> 00:20:40,900
I need to note them
on the transfer papers.

308
00:20:42,260 --> 00:20:43,790
You want to take prisoners?

309
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:45,280
What business does your Huai'an Guard have

310
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:47,700
with the men who caused trouble
at the dam here?

311
00:20:47,700 --> 00:20:49,400
Didn't our guard lend you the men

312
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:51,600
to suppress the riot in the first place?

313
00:20:51,900 --> 00:20:52,980
Do we really need to

314
00:20:53,440 --> 00:20:55,700
waste our breath on you just to take them?

315
00:21:09,360 --> 00:21:10,360
Come with me then.

316
00:21:41,690 --> 00:21:42,950
I'll beat you to death!

317
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:43,930
Come in.

318
00:22:01,090 --> 00:22:01,740
Wait here.

319
00:22:01,740 --> 00:22:03,540
I'll go bring out the prisoners.

320
00:22:03,740 --> 00:22:04,210
Boss.

321
00:22:04,460 --> 00:22:05,520
What are you doing?

322
00:22:06,110 --> 00:22:07,880
The Huai'an Guard sent someone to take

323
00:22:07,880 --> 00:22:09,960
the criminals
who caused trouble at the dam.

324
00:22:09,960 --> 00:22:11,620
Those were brought by Mr. Xue.

325
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:12,990
If you let them take the prisoners,

326
00:22:12,990 --> 00:22:14,040
how am I supposed to explain it to him?

327
00:22:14,040 --> 00:22:15,840
They have an official document.

328
00:22:18,720 --> 00:22:19,480
Look.

329
00:22:21,090 --> 00:22:22,820
So what if they have a document?

330
00:22:23,050 --> 00:22:23,980
What document?

331
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:25,610
Where is it?

332
00:22:25,780 --> 00:22:26,670
No papers,

333
00:22:26,830 --> 00:22:29,260
and you're going to
let them take the prisoners?

334
00:22:29,260 --> 00:22:30,720
You're asking for trouble.

335
00:22:30,720 --> 00:22:32,720
You dare to tear up an official document
from the Huai'an Guard?

336
00:22:32,720 --> 00:22:33,300
Is that so?

337
00:22:33,300 --> 00:22:34,760
Wang Teng is already dead.

338
00:22:35,010 --> 00:22:37,410
How can you people
still act so arrogantly?

339
00:22:37,780 --> 00:22:39,650
Don't make me arrest you!

340
00:22:39,780 --> 00:22:40,840
What are you doing?

341
00:22:40,990 --> 00:22:42,050
What are you doing?

342
00:22:42,740 --> 00:22:43,370
This is

343
00:22:43,930 --> 00:22:45,520
the Huai'an Branch
of the Ministry of Justice.

344
00:22:45,520 --> 00:22:46,700
You soldiers had better

345
00:22:46,700 --> 00:22:48,240
stop throwing your weight around here.

346
00:22:48,240 --> 00:22:48,850
I

347
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:51,500
recognize only documents
issued by the Ministry of Justice.

348
00:22:51,500 --> 00:22:53,500
Then I'll flatten this whole place!

349
00:22:53,760 --> 00:22:54,520
Big talk!

350
00:22:54,520 --> 00:22:55,850
That's enough, that's enough!

351
00:22:55,850 --> 00:22:57,260
Why don't you blast me with a cannon?

352
00:22:57,260 --> 00:22:58,180
Stop arguing!

353
00:23:00,010 --> 00:23:01,940
We're all serving the government.

354
00:23:02,110 --> 00:23:04,170
There's no need to fall out over this.

355
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:06,000
Let's go.

356
00:23:07,610 --> 00:23:08,480
You said it!

357
00:23:08,680 --> 00:23:09,910
I'll blast you with a cannon!

358
00:23:09,910 --> 00:23:11,650
I said it! Come on, blast me!

359
00:23:11,650 --> 00:23:12,280
Let's go!

360
00:23:12,300 --> 00:23:13,230
Have some water.

361
00:23:15,770 --> 00:23:16,290
Here.

362
00:23:18,390 --> 00:23:18,990
Dingyuan.

363
00:23:19,480 --> 00:23:20,610
Where have you been?

364
00:23:25,740 --> 00:23:26,680
You must be Yulu.

365
00:23:28,460 --> 00:23:29,850
This is Dr. Su.

366
00:23:30,780 --> 00:23:31,870
Nice to meet you, Dr. Su.

367
00:23:31,870 --> 00:23:32,360
Yulu,

368
00:23:32,510 --> 00:23:33,710
go prepare some food.

369
00:23:52,980 --> 00:23:54,790
Envoy, we failed to get him out.

370
00:23:59,740 --> 00:24:01,060
What do we do now?

371
00:24:01,220 --> 00:24:02,950
That place is heavily guarded.

372
00:24:04,130 --> 00:24:05,850
I underestimated the difficulty.

373
00:24:05,850 --> 00:24:07,940
Getting him out won't be easy.

374
00:24:14,480 --> 00:24:15,280
Miss Su.

375
00:24:17,940 --> 00:24:18,430
And you're...

376
00:24:18,430 --> 00:24:19,240
Zuo Yehe.

377
00:24:21,600 --> 00:24:23,660
She's the Envoy of the Iron Alliance.

378
00:24:27,180 --> 00:24:28,870
This official uniform
won't do the job, huh?

379
00:24:28,870 --> 00:24:30,670
It's enough to get you arrested.

380
00:24:36,650 --> 00:24:38,780
Uncle Liang, carry on with your thing.

381
00:24:38,870 --> 00:24:40,000
Don't frighten him.

382
00:24:42,180 --> 00:24:43,310
Have you had enough?

383
00:24:43,930 --> 00:24:44,960
I got you the information you wanted,

384
00:24:44,960 --> 00:24:46,360
and I even lent you my men.

385
00:24:46,570 --> 00:24:47,930
What about your promise

386
00:24:47,950 --> 00:24:49,150
to go to Jinan with me?

387
00:24:51,780 --> 00:24:53,370
But I can't go with you yet.

388
00:24:53,630 --> 00:24:56,030
You keep putting off
going to Jinan with us.

389
00:24:56,280 --> 00:24:59,610
Isn't it just to escort
the Crown Prince back to the capital?

390
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:01,600
Then I might as well kill him.

391
00:25:02,170 --> 00:25:04,030
That way, you'll finally give up.

392
00:25:06,480 --> 00:25:07,440
Can you

393
00:25:07,810 --> 00:25:08,870
help me rescue him?

394
00:25:10,350 --> 00:25:12,950
If you do, I'll definitely
go with you to Jinan.

395
00:25:13,500 --> 00:25:15,760
Even if we don't save the Crown Prince...

396
00:25:16,200 --> 00:25:18,330
Even if we don't save the Crown Prince,

397
00:25:18,830 --> 00:25:21,110
I can still take you there.

398
00:25:28,540 --> 00:25:29,740
This is the last time.

399
00:25:43,140 --> 00:25:44,210
I have a way

400
00:25:44,230 --> 00:25:45,890
to help Your Highness escape.

401
00:25:57,930 --> 00:25:59,390
If you have a way to escape,

402
00:25:59,930 --> 00:26:01,260
why don't you all use it?

403
00:26:03,590 --> 00:26:04,610
They all have families to look after,

404
00:26:04,610 --> 00:26:06,150
and we've lived here all our lives.

405
00:26:06,150 --> 00:26:07,410
Where could we run to?

406
00:26:08,240 --> 00:26:10,370
There's just something
I've been wanting to say,

407
00:26:10,370 --> 00:26:12,230
but I'm not sure whether I should.

408
00:26:14,280 --> 00:26:15,080
Speak freely.

409
00:26:18,650 --> 00:26:20,380
After Emperor Yongle took the throne,

410
00:26:20,380 --> 00:26:21,640
he built Beijing city,

411
00:26:23,170 --> 00:26:26,020
campaigned against the Mongols in the north
and against Jiaozhi in the south,

412
00:26:26,020 --> 00:26:28,150
opened the Grand Canal,
sent fleets abroad,

413
00:26:28,150 --> 00:26:30,610
and later compiled the great encyclopedia.

414
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:33,520
Each of these
was a monumental achievement,

415
00:26:33,890 --> 00:26:35,090
but behind each

416
00:26:35,780 --> 00:26:38,580
lay a vast demand
for labor, materials, and money.

417
00:26:38,720 --> 00:26:40,920
Take Huai'an Prefecture, where I live.

418
00:26:41,220 --> 00:26:43,580
Besides the usual land tax,

419
00:26:43,610 --> 00:26:45,540
paper-note tax, and salt tax,

420
00:26:45,570 --> 00:26:48,850
there are surcharges
under countless names,

421
00:26:48,880 --> 00:26:50,480
and new ones keep appearing.

422
00:26:52,670 --> 00:26:54,670
We common people truly suffer.

423
00:26:56,330 --> 00:26:59,460
After my father ascended the throne,
he lightened taxes

424
00:26:59,860 --> 00:27:02,860
and sought to
let the people recover and live in peace.

425
00:27:03,240 --> 00:27:04,370
Why, then, do you

426
00:27:05,650 --> 00:27:07,210
bear such a heavy burden?

427
00:27:12,050 --> 00:27:15,510
Your Highness, if you can understand
the reasons behind this,

428
00:27:18,710 --> 00:27:21,510
you'll surely become
a wise and benevolent ruler.

429
00:27:23,310 --> 00:27:25,130
We commoners will be fortunate indeed.

430
00:27:25,130 --> 00:27:25,790
Kong Shiba,

431
00:27:25,930 --> 00:27:26,490
come out!

432
00:27:31,190 --> 00:27:32,250
What are you doing?

433
00:27:32,780 --> 00:27:33,910
Behave yourselves.

434
00:27:39,500 --> 00:27:40,630
Behave yourselves!

435
00:27:45,810 --> 00:27:47,000
I'll go first.

436
00:28:05,230 --> 00:28:06,360
Is everything okay?

437
00:28:06,440 --> 00:28:07,170
Don't worry.

438
00:28:09,240 --> 00:28:09,960
Take care.

439
00:28:11,050 --> 00:28:11,650
It's fine.

440
00:28:12,280 --> 00:28:13,010
Don't worry.

441
00:28:13,140 --> 00:28:14,070
I'll go with him.

442
00:28:17,220 --> 00:28:18,020
Stop looking.

443
00:28:20,190 --> 00:28:20,760
Hurry!

444
00:28:24,630 --> 00:28:25,370
Hurry up!

445
00:28:38,480 --> 00:28:40,210
Quit acting tough. Get inside!

446
00:28:40,590 --> 00:28:41,410
You're here.

447
00:28:42,460 --> 00:28:43,040
Sit.

448
00:28:44,780 --> 00:28:46,330
Look at you, at your age,

449
00:28:47,070 --> 00:28:48,250
getting yourself into this mess.

450
00:28:48,250 --> 00:28:50,170
You really brought this upon yourself.

451
00:28:50,170 --> 00:28:52,630
Weren't you deliberately shortchanging us

452
00:28:52,870 --> 00:28:54,660
on our rations to drive us to revolt?

453
00:28:54,660 --> 00:28:55,700
Then you'd have the perfect excuse

454
00:28:55,700 --> 00:28:57,170
to get rid of all of us

455
00:28:57,170 --> 00:28:58,230
who know the truth.

456
00:29:01,350 --> 00:29:03,400
You're not senile, old man.

457
00:29:04,450 --> 00:29:05,020
Come on.

458
00:29:06,460 --> 00:29:07,000
Sit.

459
00:29:11,130 --> 00:29:13,130
You knew what you were getting into,

460
00:29:13,410 --> 00:29:14,610
yet you did it anyway.

461
00:29:15,310 --> 00:29:16,840
You must've come prepared.

462
00:29:24,040 --> 00:29:25,110
My last meal, huh?

463
00:29:27,940 --> 00:29:28,890
Xue Baguan,

464
00:29:30,050 --> 00:29:31,760
I originally came here hoping to

465
00:29:31,760 --> 00:29:33,280
negotiate terms with you.

466
00:29:35,090 --> 00:29:36,790
But now I've changed my mind.

467
00:29:42,960 --> 00:29:43,930
Old man,

468
00:29:44,780 --> 00:29:46,300
throughout history,

469
00:29:47,240 --> 00:29:49,170
so many people have died unjustly.

470
00:29:51,150 --> 00:29:53,010
One more won't make a difference.

471
00:29:54,090 --> 00:29:55,200
Do as you please.

472
00:29:56,760 --> 00:29:58,560
Do whatever you want.

473
00:30:00,090 --> 00:30:00,720
Tie him up.

474
00:30:03,570 --> 00:30:04,290
Stay still!

475
00:30:08,700 --> 00:30:09,930
Old soldier.

476
00:30:10,830 --> 00:30:11,890
Good that you know.

477
00:30:11,980 --> 00:30:13,370
Today, I'd like to see

478
00:30:13,810 --> 00:30:16,480
just how tough you really are.

479
00:30:17,760 --> 00:30:18,720
Xue Baguan,

480
00:30:18,900 --> 00:30:20,090
even if it costs my life,

481
00:30:20,090 --> 00:30:22,480
I'll expose all your filthy dealings

482
00:30:22,830 --> 00:30:24,520
and let the whole world know!

483
00:30:26,650 --> 00:30:27,980
Drink this bowl of wine,

484
00:30:28,720 --> 00:30:30,580
and you can say whatever you like.

485
00:30:33,070 --> 00:30:34,310
You won't...

486
00:31:08,700 --> 00:31:09,330
Kong?

487
00:31:10,370 --> 00:31:10,930
Kong.

488
00:31:11,570 --> 00:31:12,650
-Kong!
-Kong!

489
00:31:12,650 --> 00:31:13,150
Kong.

490
00:31:13,180 --> 00:31:15,760
-Kong!
-Kong!

491
00:31:15,890 --> 00:31:17,170
-Kong!
-Kong!

492
00:31:17,610 --> 00:31:18,200
Come on.

493
00:31:20,670 --> 00:31:21,560
Hurry, carry him in.

494
00:31:21,560 --> 00:31:22,280
Kong.

495
00:31:31,230 --> 00:31:32,990
I'm fine. I'm fine.

496
00:31:37,170 --> 00:31:38,330
Where is Hong?

497
00:31:42,280 --> 00:31:44,590
Call Hong over.

498
00:31:45,960 --> 00:31:46,720
Hong Wang,

499
00:31:47,430 --> 00:31:48,560
Kong is calling you.

500
00:31:48,880 --> 00:31:50,480
You guys go over there first.

501
00:32:21,460 --> 00:32:24,860
Your Highness, when you were beating up
Xue Baguan at the dam,

502
00:32:25,570 --> 00:32:27,770
you could've slipped away in the chaos.

503
00:32:29,500 --> 00:32:30,810
Why did you

504
00:32:31,240 --> 00:32:33,210
risk your life to rush over?

505
00:32:44,240 --> 00:32:47,100
Though his rank is low,
he's still a court official.

506
00:32:49,970 --> 00:32:53,030
How could I let him run wild,
committing such outrages?

507
00:32:59,850 --> 00:33:01,200
After I die,

508
00:33:04,240 --> 00:33:06,130
they'll come to collect my body.

509
00:33:06,760 --> 00:33:08,120
When that happens, you...

510
00:33:08,120 --> 00:33:09,720
you disguise yourself as me.

511
00:33:10,480 --> 00:33:12,140
Switch places with my corpse,

512
00:33:14,250 --> 00:33:15,920
and you'll be able to escape.

513
00:33:23,560 --> 00:33:25,360
So this is the way you mentioned?

514
00:33:26,810 --> 00:33:28,040
To be honest,

515
00:33:30,720 --> 00:33:32,440
I'm trading my life for yours

516
00:33:33,720 --> 00:33:35,810
not because of your identity,

517
00:33:37,930 --> 00:33:40,960
but because when you fought alongside us,

518
00:33:41,430 --> 00:33:44,110
I saw a different kind of light

519
00:33:45,140 --> 00:33:47,380
in your eyes.

520
00:33:56,520 --> 00:33:57,410
Hey,

521
00:33:58,000 --> 00:33:59,090
Second Brother Ding.

522
00:33:58,730 --> 00:34:02,020
[Tracker Ding Zhengde]

523
00:34:02,460 --> 00:34:03,090
Kong.

524
00:34:03,850 --> 00:34:05,040
Listen.

525
00:34:06,150 --> 00:34:09,120
Xue Baguan took my army tag.

526
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:12,730
You must get it back for me.

527
00:34:13,409 --> 00:34:14,139
Understood.

528
00:34:20,409 --> 00:34:21,820
That tag

529
00:34:23,330 --> 00:34:25,690
must stay with me.

530
00:34:57,600 --> 00:34:58,250
Kong.

531
00:34:58,780 --> 00:34:59,390
Kong!

532
00:35:27,090 --> 00:35:27,780
Kong...

533
00:35:28,350 --> 00:35:35,530
♪ The Bian River flows,
the Si River flows ♪

534
00:35:36,520 --> 00:35:43,590
♪ Converging at
the ancient Guazhou Ferry ♪

535
00:35:41,100 --> 00:35:41,690
Fang.

536
00:35:44,510 --> 00:35:52,170
♪ The Bian River flows,
the Si River flows ♪

537
00:35:47,230 --> 00:35:48,360
I've searched Li Dam

538
00:35:49,120 --> 00:35:51,330
inside and out, top to bottom,

539
00:35:52,270 --> 00:35:53,930
but my friend is
still nowhere to be found.

540
00:35:52,720 --> 00:36:00,410
♪ Converging at
the ancient Guazhou Ferry ♪

541
00:35:55,290 --> 00:35:56,690
It's not surprising.

542
00:35:57,750 --> 00:35:58,890
Huai'an has been

543
00:35:59,460 --> 00:36:01,330
in complete chaos these past few days.

544
00:36:01,330 --> 00:36:03,730
First, there was your 400-liao grain ship,

545
00:36:03,810 --> 00:36:05,670
smashed to pieces in a collision.

546
00:36:05,940 --> 00:36:06,600
Yesterday,

547
00:36:06,710 --> 00:36:07,940
Commander Wang of the Huai'an Guard

548
00:36:07,940 --> 00:36:10,400
was poisoned to death
at his family banquet.

549
00:36:13,930 --> 00:36:16,730
Wasn't that around the time
I came looking for you?

550
00:36:17,600 --> 00:36:19,000
Who poisoned him?

551
00:36:19,290 --> 00:36:20,710
According to the coroner,

552
00:36:20,710 --> 00:36:22,370
a Yangzhou specialty dessert

553
00:36:22,640 --> 00:36:24,170
contained a deadly poison.

554
00:36:24,640 --> 00:36:26,350
There was no immediate reaction

555
00:36:26,350 --> 00:36:27,550
after the first bite,

556
00:36:27,640 --> 00:36:29,170
so no one suspected a thing.

557
00:36:29,580 --> 00:36:30,960
It wasn't until the banquet was
nearly over

558
00:36:30,960 --> 00:36:31,770
that the poison took effect.

559
00:36:31,770 --> 00:36:32,900
And within moments,

560
00:36:33,730 --> 00:36:34,790
Lord Wang was dead.

561
00:36:35,460 --> 00:36:38,120
The poisoner's method was really bizarre.

562
00:36:38,740 --> 00:36:39,890
There were several tables of guests,

563
00:36:39,890 --> 00:36:42,330
yet Lord Wang was the only one who died.

564
00:36:44,100 --> 00:36:44,660
Oh, right.

565
00:36:44,660 --> 00:36:45,890
What are you doing?

566
00:36:46,040 --> 00:36:46,810
That day at the dam,

567
00:36:46,810 --> 00:36:48,470
you arrested 10 ringleaders.

568
00:36:48,850 --> 00:36:50,140
Where are they being held now?

569
00:36:50,140 --> 00:36:51,940
The Ministry of Justice Branch.

570
00:36:53,060 --> 00:36:54,120
Take me to see them.

571
00:36:54,250 --> 00:36:56,110
I want to identify them one by one.

572
00:37:01,630 --> 00:37:02,430
Young Master,

573
00:37:02,770 --> 00:37:04,300
I have something to report.

574
00:37:04,910 --> 00:37:05,520
Go ahead.

575
00:37:05,980 --> 00:37:07,960
Before the ships collided
at the dam that day,

576
00:37:07,960 --> 00:37:10,080
someone saw a fight
break out aboard one of the ships.

577
00:37:10,080 --> 00:37:12,160
One of the men was tall and burly.

578
00:37:12,440 --> 00:37:13,570
It was Liang Xingfu.

579
00:37:22,500 --> 00:37:24,220
Liang Xingfu of the Iron Alliance?

580
00:37:24,220 --> 00:37:25,410
Without a doubt.

581
00:37:25,860 --> 00:37:27,410
Zhu Zhanji is already in Huai'an,

582
00:37:27,410 --> 00:37:29,790
and the Iron Alliance
is still pestering him.

583
00:37:29,790 --> 00:37:31,330
This is not what Father

584
00:37:31,330 --> 00:37:33,000
agreed upon with them.

585
00:37:35,710 --> 00:37:36,710
Send word to them.

586
00:37:37,830 --> 00:37:39,120
If the dog won't obey,

587
00:37:39,940 --> 00:37:41,630
its master won't go easy on it.

588
00:37:42,020 --> 00:37:43,440
Dare to think otherwise,

589
00:37:44,250 --> 00:37:45,980
and you'll pay with your lives.

590
00:37:46,040 --> 00:37:46,770
Yes, yes.

591
00:37:47,640 --> 00:37:48,500
One more thing.

592
00:37:49,080 --> 00:37:52,480
I've also looked into
the troublemaking trackers being held

593
00:37:52,750 --> 00:37:53,830
at the Ministry of Justice Branch here.

594
00:37:53,830 --> 00:37:55,430
None of them appear suspicious.

595
00:37:55,430 --> 00:37:56,360
Here's the list.

596
00:38:04,560 --> 00:38:05,480
Hong Wang.

597
00:38:11,500 --> 00:38:12,930
You idiot!

598
00:38:13,370 --> 00:38:16,930
Hong stands in for Zhu, and Wang for Zhan!
Hong Wang is Zhu Zhanji!

599
00:38:16,930 --> 00:38:19,210
Surround the Huai'an Branch at once!

600
00:38:19,230 --> 00:38:20,730
Bring Hong Wang to me!

601
00:38:20,730 --> 00:38:21,370
Yes.

602
00:38:22,460 --> 00:38:23,000
Yes.

603
00:38:37,870 --> 00:38:38,870
Bring the body up.

604
00:38:54,690 --> 00:38:56,160
Shouldn't we examine the body?

605
00:38:56,160 --> 00:38:58,420
If you want to, go ahead.
I'm not doing it.

606
00:39:08,000 --> 00:39:08,480
Come on.

607
00:39:08,540 --> 00:39:09,160
Get out!

608
00:39:09,890 --> 00:39:10,950
What are you doing?

609
00:39:11,100 --> 00:39:12,300
Have you all gone mad?

610
00:39:15,040 --> 00:39:15,640
Stop!

611
00:39:17,040 --> 00:39:17,660
Get down!

612
00:39:18,620 --> 00:39:19,120
Down!

613
00:39:19,190 --> 00:39:20,230
-Down!
-Behave!

614
00:39:22,920 --> 00:39:23,850
You dare defy us?

615
00:39:24,160 --> 00:39:24,730
Get down!

616
00:39:25,370 --> 00:39:26,370
Stay down!

617
00:39:39,690 --> 00:39:40,370
Make way!

618
00:39:40,810 --> 00:39:41,640
-Kong.
-Kong.

619
00:39:41,640 --> 00:39:42,480
Kong.

620
00:39:42,830 --> 00:39:43,600
Kong.

621
00:39:43,690 --> 00:39:44,500
Kong!

622
00:39:44,500 --> 00:39:45,290
Kong!

623
00:39:45,410 --> 00:39:46,890
-Kong!
-Kong!

624
00:39:47,080 --> 00:39:48,120
Kong!

625
00:39:48,290 --> 00:39:49,090
Shut the gate.

626
00:39:54,710 --> 00:39:55,410
Kong!

627
00:40:34,070 --> 00:40:34,870
Open the gate.

628
00:40:41,450 --> 00:40:41,970
Please.

629
00:40:53,960 --> 00:40:54,640
Tingyi.

630
00:40:55,660 --> 00:40:57,590
Is the one you're looking for here?

631
00:40:57,810 --> 00:40:58,740
Raise your head.

632
00:40:59,410 --> 00:41:00,080
Raise it.

633
00:41:22,230 --> 00:41:22,800
How about this?

634
00:41:22,800 --> 00:41:25,290
I'll ask the Assistant Prefect of Huai'an
to issue another order

635
00:41:25,290 --> 00:41:26,690
to expand the search area.

636
00:41:26,690 --> 00:41:27,330
Okay.

637
00:41:31,690 --> 00:41:32,620
Thank you, Fang.

638
00:41:53,270 --> 00:41:56,870
The Yong'an Battalion brought back
10 ringleaders from the dam.

639
00:41:57,120 --> 00:41:58,520
Why are there only 8 here?

640
00:42:00,100 --> 00:42:00,700
Come here!

641
00:42:01,210 --> 00:42:02,210
We're asking you.

642
00:42:02,640 --> 00:42:03,290
Answer us.

643
00:42:05,830 --> 00:42:06,830
They are all here.

644
00:42:08,290 --> 00:42:09,420
Why are there only 8?

645
00:42:09,440 --> 00:42:11,270
Weren't they being held together?

646
00:42:11,270 --> 00:42:13,530
One of them died. They took the body away.

647
00:42:19,970 --> 00:42:20,770
Open the gate.

648
00:42:21,040 --> 00:42:21,840
Open the gate!

649
00:42:22,640 --> 00:42:23,440
Open the gate!

650
00:42:35,810 --> 00:42:36,690
Where

651
00:42:37,120 --> 00:42:38,380
did you get this thing?

652
00:42:38,890 --> 00:42:41,240
It's a siege cannon
left over from the Jingnan Campaign.

653
00:42:41,240 --> 00:42:42,800
The Iron Alliance had hidden
several of them back then.

654
00:42:42,800 --> 00:42:45,860
They have been kept
by Tie Xuan's former subordinates.

655
00:42:50,120 --> 00:42:51,780
Where is the other one? Speak!

656
00:43:02,740 --> 00:43:03,440
A bit more to the left.
